From 48d77bd9dd3c58aef82e100055238d823df928b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:49:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat(control-plane): add a fake launcher serving an
 OpenAI-compatible stub

CI and local development need deployments that reach Ready and answer
requests through the gateway without GPUs or model weights.

FakeLauncher starts one asyncio HTTP server per instance on an
ephemeral port, inside the control plane's event loop and with the
standard library only (no threads). Each instance answers GET /health
and POST /v1/chat/completions: with "stream": true an SSE stream of
chat.completion.chunk events ending with "data: [DONE]", otherwise one
chat.completion object; the reply names the instance. Requests are
bounded (Content-Length up to 1 MiB, 30 s to read) and get OpenAI-style
errors. The listen address and the host written into instance urls are
separate, so a container can listen on 0.0.0.0 and advertise its
compose service name. stop() closes the server and cancels requests in
flight, releasing the port; aclose() stops every instance; verify()
fails at once for instances it does not know, e.g. after a restart.

network.py holds what the process launcher will share: bind and
advertise host validation, instance urls, and a GET /health probe over
asyncio streams that never goes through an HTTP proxy.
